The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-watch-series-12-announced-all-day-hr-sensor/">Apple Watch Series 12</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-watch-ultra-4-announced-battery-life/">Apple Watch Ultra 4</a> bring new health sensors, a new chip, and more detailed recovery insights to Apple's smartwatch lineup, so how do they compare?<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/apple-watch-series-12-vs-apple-watch-ultra-4.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066173" /><br/>
Both models feature the S11 chip, 4GB of RAM, 64GB of storage, and the new Health Sensing System, which measures heart rate every five seconds throughout the day. They also share Readiness, Recovery HRV, daytime vitals, improved step tracking, hypertension notifications, sleep apnea notifications, Sleep Score, and more. This means that the Ultra 4's higher price does not buy you more advanced everyday health tracking.<br/>
<br/>
The Apple Watch Series 12 starts at &#36;399, while the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-watch-ultra/">Apple Watch Ultra 4</a> starts at &#36;799. The gap narrows if you want a premium case material, with the titanium Series 12 starting at &#36;699. This year, the Series 12 also gains a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-watch-series-12-comes-new-finishes/">ceramic option</a> starting at &#36;899, making it more expensive than the Ultra despite its smaller size and shorter battery life.<br/>
<br/>
